<section id="description-section" class="product-anchor-section">
        <h1>Description</h1>
        <div>
          <p><b>Oxy-Acetylene Cylinder Cart</b>&nbsp;is a workshop cart designed for storing and transporting a set of gas cylinders together with the required equipment. The structure is designed to be fabricated in-house from standard steel materials and commonly available components.</p>

<h3>Why build this cylinder cart?</h3>
<p></p>

<ul class="dots">
    <li>
        <p><b>One frame for the complete set:</b>&nbsp;The oxygen and acetylene cylinders are carried on a common frame, making the setup easier to organize and move around the workshop.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>Stable cylinder support:</b>&nbsp;The structure provides a solid base for the cylinders and allows them to be secured to the frame.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>Space for equipment:</b>&nbsp;The cart makes it easier to organize hoses and the basic equipment used with an oxy-acetylene setup.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>Steel workshop construction:</b>&nbsp;The project is based on a welded steel structure intended for normal workshop use.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>Designed for DIY fabrication:</b>&nbsp;The documentation includes the information required to prepare the parts and assemble the complete cart.</p>
    </li>
</ul>

            <h3>What does this project include?</h3>

          <ul class="dots">
                 <li>
                  <p><b>PDF fabrication drawings:</b>&nbsp;Technical drawings with the dimensions required to prepare the parts and verify fabrication.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>DXF files:</b>&nbsp;Ready-to-use files for parts intended for laser or plasma cutting.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Assembly instructions:</b>&nbsp;Assembly views showing the sequence and method of joining the individual components.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Material list:</b>&nbsp;A list of profiles, plates, fasteners, wheels and other components required to build the cart.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>3D views:</b>&nbsp;Views of the complete structure and its details to make fabrication and assembly easier to understand.</p>
                </li>
          </ul>

        <div class="product-note">
  <p class="product-note__title">ℹ️ Digital Product (DIY Plans)</p>
  <p>This product is digital documentation for building an oxy-acetylene cylinder cart yourself. It does not include a finished cart, cylinders, equipment or metal parts. Building the structure requires basic workshop equipment and skills in steel fabrication and welding.</p>
</div>
      </section>









